 "notes": "The southern double reef: entry over broken rocks, a sandy shelf to the drop-off at about 10 m, the inner reef sloping to about 20 m, the sand valley between the reefs that gives the site its name at 18-24 m with garden eels and rays, and the outer reef beyond (bonaire.com site 42, zentacle.com reviews). Band widths agree with the Hilma Hooker, which OpenStreetMap places 370 m south in the same sand channel; the 30 m contour, the mooring spot and the route direction are assumptions. Coastline, pier and dive-site markers © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
